"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin `layout.spl`'s block layout (`layout_tree` -> `_layout_block_node`,
the path used by `browser_renderer` and `engine_merge`) to Chrome 159 for the
three box-model rules already fixed in `layout_core.spl` (PR #9812):
content-box `width`/`height`, `box-sizing:border-box`, adjoining sibling margin
collapse, and a bordered parent keeping its content width.
Audience: browser-engine layout maintainers.

Chrome oracle: the same pages and numbers as
`layout_core_block_flex_chrome159_spec.spl` (Chrome for Testing 159.0.8154.6,
`--headless --no-sandbox --window-size=900,2000 --dump-dom`, 2026-11-16;
`html,body` margin 0, parent `width:300px; margin:0`, child geometry is
`getBoundingClientRect()` relative to the parent):

| case | child style(s) | Chrome child x,y,w,h | Chrome parent h |
|------|----------------|----------------------|-----------------|
| a | `margin-left:10px;margin-right:20px;height:30px` | 10,0,270,30 | 30 |
| a-width | `width:100px;margin-left:10px;margin-right:20px;height:30px` | 10,0,100,30 | 30 |
| a-nested | parent `border:5px solid`; n1 `height:20px;margin-left:7px` > n2 `height:10px;margin:0 4px 0 3px;padding:2px` | n1 12,5,293,20; n2 15,5,286,14 | 30 |
| f | `height:20px` + `display:none;height:99px;margin-top:40px` + `height:30px` | f3 at y=20 | 50 |
| f-collapse | `height:20px;margin-bottom:10px` + `display:none;margin-top:50px` + `height:30px;margin-top:15px` | g3 at y=35 | 65 |
| b | `width:100px;padding:10px;height:20px` | 0,0,120,40 | 40 |
| auto-both | `width:100px;margin:0 auto;height:30px` | 100,0,100,30 | 30 |
| auto-left | `width:100px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:20px;height:30px` | 180,0,100,30 | 30 |
| auto-right | `width:100px;margin-left:10px;margin-right:auto;height:30px` | 10,0,100,30 | 30 |
| auto-width | `margin:auto;height:30px` | 0,0,300,30 | 30 |
| auto-single | `width:100px;margin:auto;height:30px` | 100,0,100,30 | 30 |
| auto-overconstrained | `width:400px;margin:0 auto;height:30px` | 0,0,400,30 | 30 |
| auto-nested | parent `border:5px solid`; child `width:100px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding:10px;height:20px` | 95,5,120,40 | 50 |
| auto-4value | `width:100px;margin:5px auto 0 20px;height:30px` (inside a flow-root wrapper) | 20,5,100,30 (the 5px top margin collapses through the parent: parent y=5) | 30 (wrapper 35) |
| none-root | root `display:none;width:300px;height:40px;margin:0 auto` | root 0,0,0,0 | — |
| c | `height:50px;padding:5px` | 0,0,300,60 | 60 |
| d | `height:20px;margin-bottom:10px` + `height:30px;margin-top:15px` | d2 at y=35 | 65 |
| e | `height:20px` + `height:30px` | e2 at y=20 | 50 |
| border | parent `border:5px solid`; child `height:20px` | 5,5,300,20 | 30 (border box 310 wide) |

border-box floor: `box-sizing:border-box;width:50px;height:5px;padding:5px`
gives 0,0,50,10 in Chrome 159 (row `border_box_height_floor`,
doc/08_tracking/bug/web_layout_cascade_selector_paint_chrome159_round4_divergences_2026-11-15.md).

Rows a-width, a-nested, f (with margin-top) and f-collapse were measured with
the same Chrome binary and page setup on 2026-11-16. Cases a, a-width, a-nested,
f and f-collapse were red before the 2026-11-16 fix (engine gave a at
0,0,300,30; a-nested n2 at 5,5,300; f and f-collapse kept the hidden child as a
third box, parent heights 189 and 115).

The auto-* and none-root rows were measured with the same Chrome binary and
page setup on 2026-11-16. auto-both, auto-left, auto-single, auto-nested,
auto-parse and none-root were red before the 2026-11-16 `margin:auto` fix (auto
margins parsed to 0 with no flag; a display:none root was laid out in full).
auto-right, auto-width, auto-overconstrained and auto-4value already passed,
because an auto margin that computes to 0 matches the old parse-as-0; they stay
as regression guards for the new auto path.

Parent/child margin collapse (`pc-*` cases, CSS 2.2 §8.3.1) was measured with
the same Chrome binary on 2026-11-16, each case inside a
`<div style="display:flow-root">` wrapper (mirrored by `_wrap`: the layout root
is a BFC root), geometry relative to the wrapper:

| case | parent > child | Chrome parent y,h / child y | wrapper h |
|------|----------------|-----------------------------|-----------|
| pc-top | P `width:300px` > C `margin-top:10px;height:20px` | 10,20 / 10 | 30 |
| pc-top-padding | P `padding-top:4px` > same C | 0,34 / 14 | 34 |
| pc-top-border | P `border:5px solid` > same C | 0,40 / 15 | 40 |
| pc-bottom-auto | P > C `height:20px;margin-bottom:10px`; sibling `height:5px` | 0,20; sibling y=30 | 35 |
| pc-bottom-padding | P `padding-bottom:4px` > same C; sibling | 0,34; sibling y=34 | 39 |
| pc-bottom-height | P `height:40px` > same C; sibling | 0,40; sibling y=40 | 45 |
| pc-nested | A `mt:4` > B `mt:12;mb:3` > C `mt:8;mb:6;height:10px` | all y=12, A h=10 | 28 |
| pc-negative | P `mt:10` > C `mt:-5` > G `mt:3;height:20px` | all y=5 | 25 |
| pc-negative-sibling | S `height:10px;mb:20` + P `mt:10` > C `mt:-30;height:10px` | P y=0, C y=0 | 10 |
| pc-flex | P `display:flex` > C `width:100px;mt:10;height:20px` | 0,30 / 10 | 30 |
| pc-overflow-hidden | P `overflow:hidden` > C `mt:10;height:20px` | 0,30 / 10 | 30 |
| pc-overflow-clip | P `overflow:clip` > same C | 10,20 / 10 | 30 |
| pc-flow-root | P `display:flow-root` > same C | 0,30 / 10 | 30 |

pc-top, pc-bottom-auto, pc-nested, pc-negative, pc-negative-sibling,
pc-overflow-clip and auto-4value were red before the 2026-11-16 fix; the blocked
cases (padding, border, height, flex, overflow:hidden, flow-root) already
passed and stay as guards.

Round 2 (`mc-*` rows, 2026-11-17, same Chrome binary and wrapper page; each
row quotes its Chrome line): collapse through empty blocks (es, en, ef, el,
ep), explicit `height:0` versus auto (h0, h0e), `min-height` (mh, mhp, mhq,
mht), per-side padding (pb, pt, ept), floats and abs boxes between or before
collapsing margins (fl, ab/abm, ff, fa), whitespace-only text (ws) and
grid/flex-column items (gr, fc). Red before the fix: es, en, ef, el, ep, h0,
h0e, mh, mhq, mht, fl, abm, ff, fa, ws, gr (16). Guards that already passed:
mhp, pb, pt, ept, fc. Chrome detail: a min-height only blocks the bottom
collapse when it raises the height (mhp keeps the collapse, mhq does not).

Per-side borders (`bw-*` rows, 2026-11-17) are pinned in the last describe
block below. Not covered here (open `_layout_block_node` divergences): clearance, the layout root's own margins, float avoidance by
following content, and `width:0`/percent widths with auto margins (width 0
means auto here, so they never centre).
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-SSPEC-BROWSER_ENGINE — layout_tree block box geometry matches Chrome 159.
"""
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.dom.{BeDomNode}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.layout.{BeLayoutBox, layout_tree}

fn _parent() -> BeDomNode:
    var p = BeDomNode.element("div")
    p.set_style("width", "300px")
    p

fn _child(height: text) -> BeDomNode:
    var c = BeDomNode.element("div")
    c.set_style("height", height)
    c

fn _lay(parent: BeDomNode) -> BeLayoutBox:
    layout_tree(parent, 900.0, 2000.0)

fn _wrap(parent: BeDomNode) -> BeDomNode:
    """Style-less layout root around `parent`, mirroring the Chrome page's
    `display:flow-root` wrapper: the root is a BFC root, so a margin that
    collapses through `parent` stays inside it and moves `parent` down."""
    var w = BeDomNode.element("div")
    w.add_child(parent)
    w

fn _block(style_pairs: [text]) -> BeDomNode:
    var d = BeDomNode.element("div")
    var i = 0
    while i + 1 < style_pairs.len():
        d.set_style(style_pairs[i], style_pairs[i + 1])
        i = i + 2
    d

describe "layout_tree block box model (Chrome 159)":
    it "case b: width is a content-box width, so padding widens the box to 120px":
        var p = _parent()
        var b = _child("20px")
        b.set_style("width", "100px")
        b.style.padding_top = 10.0
        b.style.padding_right = 10.0
        b.style.padding_bottom = 10.0
        b.style.padding_left = 10.0
        p.add_child(b)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(120.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].height).to_equal(40.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(40.0)

    it "case c: an explicit height is the content height, padding adds to the border box":
        var p = _parent()
        var c = _child("50px")
        c.style.padding_top = 5.0
        c.style.padding_right = 5.0
        c.style.padding_bottom = 5.0
        c.style.padding_left = 5.0
        p.add_child(c)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(300.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].height).to_equal(60.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(60.0)

    it "border-box: width and height are the border box, never below padding":
        var p = _parent()
        var f = _child("5px")
        f.set_style("width", "50px")
        f.set_style("box-sizing", "border-box")
        f.style.padding_top = 5.0
        f.style.padding_right = 5.0
        f.style.padding_bottom = 5.0
        f.style.padding_left = 5.0
        p.add_child(f)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(50.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].height).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].content_height).to_equal(0.0)

    it "case d: adjoining sibling margins collapse to the larger margin":
        var p = _parent()
        var d1 = _child("20px")
        d1.set_style("margin-bottom", "10px")
        var d2 = _child("30px")
        d2.set_style("margin-top", "15px")
        p.add_child(d1)
        p.add_child(d2)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[1].y).to_equal(35.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(65.0)

    it "case e: block children stack and the auto-height parent wraps them":
        var p = _parent()
        p.add_child(_child("20px"))
        p.add_child(_child("30px"))
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.children[1].y).to_equal(20.0)
        expect(box_.children[1].width).to_equal(300.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(50.0)

    it "border: a bordered parent offsets its child by the border width":
        var p = _parent()
        p.style.set_border_all(5.0, "solid")
        p.add_child(_child("20px"))
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "border: the bordered parent keeps its full 300px content width":
        var p = _parent()
        p.style.set_border_all(5.0, "solid")
        p.add_child(_child("20px"))
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(300.0)
        expect(box_.width).to_equal(310.0)

    it "case a: an auto-width block fills the container minus its horizontal margins":
        var p = _parent()
        var a = _child("30px")
        a.set_style("margin-left", "10px")
        a.set_style("margin-right", "20px")
        p.add_child(a)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(270.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].height).to_equal(30.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "case a-width: an explicit-width block sits at x + margin-left":
        var p = _parent()
        var w = _child("30px")
        w.set_style("width", "100px")
        w.set_style("margin-left", "10px")
        w.set_style("margin-right", "20px")
        p.add_child(w)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(100.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "case a-nested: horizontal margins accumulate through a bordered parent":
        var p = _parent()
        p.style.set_border_all(5.0, "solid")
        var n1 = _child("20px")
        n1.set_style("margin-left", "7px")
        var n2 = _child("10px")
        n2.set_style("margin-left", "3px")
        n2.set_style("margin-right", "4px")
        n2.style.padding_top = 2.0
        n2.style.padding_right = 2.0
        n2.style.padding_bottom = 2.0
        n2.style.padding_left = 2.0
        n1.add_child(n2)
        p.add_child(n1)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        val b1 = box_.children[0]
        expect(b1.x).to_equal(12.0)
        expect(b1.y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(b1.width).to_equal(293.0)
        expect(b1.children[0].x).to_equal(15.0)
        expect(b1.children[0].y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(b1.children[0].width).to_equal(286.0)
        expect(b1.children[0].height).to_equal(14.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "case f: a display:none child generates no box and takes no space":
        var p = _parent()
        p.add_child(_child("20px"))
        var hidden = _child("99px")
        hidden.set_style("display", "none")
        hidden.set_style("margin-top", "40px")
        p.add_child(hidden)
        p.add_child(_child("30px"))
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children.len()).to_equal(2)
        expect(box_.children[1].y).to_equal(20.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(50.0)

    it "case f-collapse: siblings around a display:none child still collapse their margins":
        var p = _parent()
        var g1 = _child("20px")
        g1.set_style("margin-bottom", "10px")
        p.add_child(g1)
        var hidden = BeDomNode.element("div")
        hidden.set_style("display", "none")
        hidden.set_style("margin-top", "50px")
        p.add_child(hidden)
        var g3 = _child("30px")
        g3.set_style("margin-top", "15px")
        p.add_child(g3)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children.len()).to_equal(2)
        expect(box_.children[1].y).to_equal(35.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(65.0)

    it "auto-both: width:100px;margin:0 auto centres the block (leftover split equally)":
        var p = _parent()
        var c = _child("30px")
        c.set_style("width", "100px")
        c.set_style("margin", "0 auto")
        p.add_child(c)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(100.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(100.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "auto-left: only margin-left auto takes all the leftover space":
        var p = _parent()
        var c = _child("30px")
        c.set_style("width", "100px")
        c.set_style("margin-left", "auto")
        c.set_style("margin-right", "20px")
        p.add_child(c)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(180.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(100.0)

    it "auto-right: only margin-right auto leaves the block at margin-left":
        var p = _parent()
        var c = _child("30px")
        c.set_style("width", "100px")
        c.set_style("margin-left", "10px")
        c.set_style("margin-right", "auto")
        p.add_child(c)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(100.0)

    it "auto-width: auto margins on an auto-width block compute to 0":
        var p = _parent()
        var c = _child("30px")
        c.set_style("margin", "auto")
        p.add_child(c)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(300.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "auto-single: margin:auto with an explicit width centres like 0 auto":
        var p = _parent()
        var c = _child("30px")
        c.set_style("width", "100px")
        c.set_style("margin", "auto")
        p.add_child(c)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(100.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].y).to_equal(0.0)

    it "auto-overconstrained: a block wider than its container gets 0 auto margins":
        var p = _parent()
        var c = _child("30px")
        c.set_style("width", "400px")
        c.set_style("margin", "0 auto")
        p.add_child(c)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(400.0)

    it "auto-nested: a padded block centres inside a bordered parent's content box":
        var p = _parent()
        p.style.set_border_all(5.0, "solid")
        var c = _child("20px")
        c.set_style("width", "100px")
        c.set_style("margin-left", "auto")
        c.set_style("margin-right", "auto")
        c.set_style("padding", "10px")
        p.add_child(c)
        val box_ = _lay(p)
        expect(box_.children[0].x).to_equal(95.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].width).to_equal(120.0)
        expect(box_.children[0].height).to_equal(40.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(50.0)

    it "auto-4value: margin:5px auto 0 20px keeps the 20px left and the right auto":
        var p = _parent()
        var c = _child("30px")
        c.set_style("width", "100px")
        c.set_style("margin", "5px auto 0 20px")
        p.add_child(c)
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.children[0].x).to_equal(20.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].width).to_equal(100.0)
        # Chrome collapses the 5px top margin through the parent: both boxes
        # sit at y=5, the parent stays 30 tall, the wrapper grows to 35.
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(pb.height).to_equal(30.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(35.0)

    it "auto-parse: the margin shorthand and longhands record auto per side":
        var a = BeDomNode.element("div")
        a.set_style("margin", "0 auto")
        expect(a.style.margin_left_auto).to_equal(true)
        expect(a.style.margin_right_auto).to_equal(true)
        var b = BeDomNode.element("div")
        b.set_style("margin", "1px 2px 3px 4px")
        expect(b.style.margin_left_auto).to_equal(false)
        expect(b.style.margin_right_auto).to_equal(false)
        expect(b.style.margin_top).to_equal(1.0)
        expect(b.style.margin_right).to_equal(2.0)
        expect(b.style.margin_bottom).to_equal(3.0)
        expect(b.style.margin_left).to_equal(4.0)
        var c = BeDomNode.element("div")
        c.set_style("margin-left", "auto")
        c.set_style("margin-right", "7")
        expect(c.style.margin_left_auto).to_equal(true)
        expect(c.style.margin_right_auto).to_equal(false)
        expect(c.style.margin_right).to_equal(7.0)
        c.set_style("margin-left", "3px")
        expect(c.style.margin_left_auto).to_equal(false)
        expect(c.style.margin_left).to_equal(3.0)

    it "none-root: a display:none layout root generates a 0x0 box with no children":
        var r = BeDomNode.element("div")
        r.set_style("display", "none")
        r.set_style("width", "300px")
        r.set_style("height", "40px")
        r.add_child(_child("20px"))
        val box_ = _lay(r)
        expect(box_.x).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.width).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.height).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(box_.children.len()).to_equal(0)

describe "layout_tree parent/child margin collapse (Chrome 159, CSS 2.2 §8.3.1)":
    it "pc-top: a first child's top margin collapses through an unpadded, unbordered parent":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px"])
        p.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "10px", "height", "20px"]))
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(pb.height).to_equal(20.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "pc-top-padding: padding-top keeps the child's top margin inside the parent":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px", "padding-top", "4px"])
        p.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "10px", "height", "20px"]))
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(14.0)
        expect(pb.height).to_equal(34.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(34.0)

    it "pc-top-border: a top border keeps the child's top margin inside the parent":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px", "border", "5px solid"])
        p.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "10px", "height", "20px"]))
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(15.0)
        expect(pb.height).to_equal(40.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(40.0)

    it "pc-bottom-auto: an auto-height parent passes its last child's bottom margin out":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px"])
        p.add_child(_block(["height", "20px", "margin-bottom", "10px"]))
        var root = _wrap(p)
        root.add_child(_block(["height", "5px"]))
        val w = _lay(root)
        expect(w.children[0].height).to_equal(20.0)
        expect(w.children[1].y).to_equal(30.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(35.0)

    it "pc-bottom-padding: padding-bottom keeps the last child's bottom margin inside":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px", "padding-bottom", "4px"])
        p.add_child(_block(["height", "20px", "margin-bottom", "10px"]))
        var root = _wrap(p)
        root.add_child(_block(["height", "5px"]))
        val w = _lay(root)
        expect(w.children[0].height).to_equal(34.0)
        expect(w.children[1].y).to_equal(34.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(39.0)

    it "pc-bottom-height: an explicit height blocks the bottom collapse":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px", "height", "40px"])
        p.add_child(_block(["height", "20px", "margin-bottom", "10px"]))
        var root = _wrap(p)
        root.add_child(_block(["height", "5px"]))
        val w = _lay(root)
        expect(w.children[0].height).to_equal(40.0)
        expect(w.children[1].y).to_equal(40.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(45.0)

    it "pc-nested: margins collapse through three levels, top and bottom":
        var a = _block(["margin-top", "4px"])
        var b = _block(["margin-top", "12px", "margin-bottom", "3px"])
        b.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "8px", "margin-bottom", "6px", "height", "10px"]))
        a.add_child(b)
        val w = _lay(_wrap(a))
        val ab = w.children[0]
        expect(ab.y).to_equal(12.0)
        expect(ab.children[0].y).to_equal(12.0)
        expect(ab.children[0].children[0].y).to_equal(12.0)
        expect(ab.height).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(28.0)

    it "pc-negative: a chain 10/-5/3 resolves to max positive plus most negative (5)":
        var p = _block(["margin-top", "10px"])
        var c = _block(["margin-top", "-5px"])
        c.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "3px", "height", "20px"]))
        p.add_child(c)
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].children[0].y).to_equal(5.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(25.0)

    it "pc-negative-sibling: a sibling bottom margin joins the collapsed set 20/10/-30":
        var root = BeDomNode.element("div")
        root.add_child(_block(["height", "10px", "margin-bottom", "20px"]))
        var p = _block(["margin-top", "10px"])
        p.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "-30px", "height", "10px"]))
        root.add_child(p)
        val w = _lay(root)
        expect(w.children[1].y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(w.children[1].children[0].y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(10.0)

    it "pc-flex: a flex container does not collapse with its item's margin":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px", "display", "flex"])
        p.add_child(_block(["width", "100px", "margin-top", "10px", "height", "20px"]))
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(pb.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "pc-overflow-hidden: overflow:hidden makes the parent a BFC root":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px", "overflow", "hidden"])
        p.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "10px", "height", "20px"]))
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(pb.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "pc-overflow-clip: overflow:clip is not a BFC root, so the margin still collapses":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px", "overflow", "clip"])
        p.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "10px", "height", "20px"]))
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(pb.height).to_equal(20.0)

    it "pc-flow-root: display:flow-root makes the parent a BFC root":
        var p = _block(["width", "300px", "display", "flow-root"])
        p.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "10px", "height", "20px"]))
        val w = _lay(_wrap(p))
        val pb = w.children[0]
        expect(pb.y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(pb.children[0].y).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(pb.height).to_equal(30.0)

    it "pc-html-root: the html element is a BFC root under a #document layout root":
        # Chrome 159: html{margin:0} body{margin-top:20px} > div{margin-top:10px;height:10px}
        # gives html 0,h30, body y=20 h10, div y=20 (the root element keeps
        # body's collapsed margin inside it).
        var doc = BeDomNode.document()
        var html = BeDomNode.element("html")
        var body = _block(["margin-top", "20px"])
        body.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "10px", "height", "10px"]))
        html.add_child(body)
        doc.add_child(html)
        val d = _lay(doc)
        val hb = d.children[0]
        expect(hb.y).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(hb.height).to_equal(30.0)
        expect(hb.children[0].y).to_equal(20.0)
        expect(hb.children[0].height).to_equal(10.0)
        expect(hb.children[0].children[0].y).to_equal(20.0)

    # Round 2 (2026-11-17): Chrome 159.0.8154.6, same flow-root wrapper page
    # (`--window-size=900,2000 --dump-dom`, geometry relative to the wrapper).
    # Each comment quotes the Chrome line for the case.

    it "mc-empty-sibling: an empty block's margins collapse with both neighbours":
        # Chrome: es W h=40 | es_a y=0 h=10 | es_e y=30 h=0 | es_b y=30 h=10
        var root = BeDomNode.element("div")
        root.add_child(_block(["height", "10px", "margin-bottom", "10px"]))
        root.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "20px", "margin-bottom", "5px"]))
        root.add_child(_block(["height", "10px", "margin-top", "15px"]))
        val w = _lay(root)
        expect(w.children[1].y).to_equal(30.0)
        expect(w.children[1].height).to_equal(0.0)
        expect(w.children[2].y).to_equal(30.0)
        expect(w.height).to_equal(40.0)

    it "mc-empty-negative: an empty block joins one set (10, -5, 30, 5 gives 25)":
        # Chrome: en W h=45 | en_a y=0 h=10 | en_e y=15 h=0 | en_b y=35 h=10
        var root = BeDomNode.element("div")
        root.add_child(_block(["height", "10px", "margin-bottom", "10px"]))
        root.add_child(_block(["margin-top", "-5px", "margin-bottom", "30px"]))
        root.add_child(_block(["height", "10px", "margin-top", "5px"]))
